===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|h₁nómn̥}}
From {{inh|en|enm|name}}, {{m|enm|nome}}, from {{inh|en|ang|nama}}, {{m|ang|noma}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*namō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*namô}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₁nómn̥}}.

Cognates include {{cog|stq|Noome}}, {{cog|fy|namme}}, {{cog|nl|naam}}, {{cog|de|Name}}, {{cog|da|navn}}, {{cog|sv|namn}}, {{cog|la|nōmen}} (whence {{cog|es|nombre}}), {{cog|ru|имя}}, {{cog|sa|नामन्}}. Possible cognates outside of Indo-European include {{cog|fi|nimi}} and {{cog|hu|név}}. {{doublet|en|nomen|noun}}.

